module LoanApproval where

-- LoanStatus
--   Typed status replaces the previous status : Text field. Using an ADT
--   means a typo like "Approvd" no longer compiles, and pattern matching
--   on status is exhaustive-checked by the compiler.
data LoanStatus = Approved | Rejected
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Represents the initial loan application submitted by a borrower to a bank.
--   In practice this is the point at which the lender's underwriting obligation
--   begins — the bank must assess the borrower's repayment capacity before
--   making a credit decision. The template captures the minimum information
--   needed to make that determination: who is asking, how much, from whom,
--   and the borrower's stated income.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: borrower
--   The borrower signs because they are the party initiating the credit
--   relationship and asserting that the loan amount and income are valid.
--   Making the borrower the signatory creates an on-ledger record of the
--   application that the borrower cannot later deny submitting. The bank
--   is an observer at this stage — it has not yet committed to anything.
--
-- OBSERVERS: bank
--   The bank is an observer so it can see the request and exercise the
--   ApproveRequest or RejectRequest choices. It does not co-sign at this
--   stage because the application is a unilateral act of the borrower.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   CFPB Ability-to-Repay rule (Regulation Z) — the 25% debt-to-income
--   assertion inside ApproveRequest enforces income-based eligibility
--   at the ledger interpreter level. A request whose loanAmount exceeds
--   25% of stated salary cannot produce an Approved loan.
--   BSA Section 1020.220 (Customer Identification Program) — the borrower
--   party allocation serves as the on-ledger identity record for the loan
--   applicant. In a production system this would reference a verified KYC
--   record; here it establishes the party relationship that gates all
--   subsequent choices.
template LoanRequest
  with
    bank : Party
    borrower : Party
    salary : Decimal
    loanAmount : Decimal
  where
    ensure loanAmount > 0.0 && salary > 0.0
    signatory borrower
    observer  bank

    choice ApproveRequest : ContractId Loan
      controller bank
      do
        assertMsg "Loan exceeds 25% of stated salary (CFPB Ability-to-Repay)"
          (loanAmount <= 0.25 * salary)
        create Loan with
          bank
          borrower
          loanAmount
          status = Approved

    choice RejectRequest : ContractId Loan
      controller bank
      do
        create Loan with
          bank
          borrower
          loanAmount
          status = Rejected

-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Represents the binding loan agreement between the bank and borrower,
--   created immediately upon the bank's approval or rejection decision.
--   The status field records the outcome. An Approved loan is the legal
--   instrument that authorizes disbursement; a Rejected loan is an
--   immutable record of the declined application. Both outcomes produce
--   a co-signed contract, creating an auditable record of the credit
--   decision that neither party can unilaterally alter or delete.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: bank, borrower
--   Both parties sign the Loan contract because it represents a bilateral
--   agreement — the bank's credit decision and the borrower's acceptance
--   of the terms. Dual signatories mean neither party can archive or
--   modify the loan record without the other's co-authorization, which
--   satisfies the audit trail requirement that financial institutions
--   must maintain records of credit decisions.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   No third-party observers. The loan agreement is a private bilateral
--   contract between the bank and borrower. Regulators access loan records
--   through examination rather than real-time ledger observation.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   GDPR Article 5(1)(c) — data minimization. Only the two contracting
--   parties are stakeholders; no third party receives the borrower's
--   loan amount or financial status as a side effect of contract creation.
--   CFPB Ability-to-Repay (Regulation Z) — the Approved status signals
--   that the bank has made a documented, on-ledger credit determination
--   backed by the income-based eligibility assertion above.
template Loan
  with
    bank : Party
    borrower : Party
    loanAmount : Decimal
    status : LoanStatus
  where
    signatory bank, borrower
